{"id":"CVE-2003-0986","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2006-02-27T23:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-08T02:12:35.628Z","description":"Various routines for the ppc64 architecture on Linux kernel 2.6 prior to 2.6.2 and 2.4 prior to 2.4.24 do not use the copy_from_user function when copying data from userspace to kernelspace, which crosses security boundaries and allows local users to cause a denial of service.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2004-017.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2004:017"},{"url":"http://linux.bkbits.net:8080/linux-2.6/cset%403ffcf122S7e3xPZCpibrXq6KRRjwqw","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://linux.bkbits.net:8080/linux-2.4/cset%403fdd54b3u9Eq0Wny2Nn1HGfI3pofOQ","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://oval.cisecurity.org/repository/search/definition/oval%3Aorg.mitre.oval%3Adef%3A9707","tags":["vdb-entry","signature","x_refsource_OVAL"],"name":"oval:org.mitre.oval:def:9707"}],"vendors":["linux-kernel"]}
