{"id":"CVE-2003-1161","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-05-10T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T23:52:04.269Z","description":"exit.c in Linux kernel 2.6-test9-CVS, as stored on kernel.bkbits.net, was modified to contain a backdoor, which could allow local users to elevate their privileges by passing __WCLONE|__WALL to the sys_wait4 function.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.ussg.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/0311.0/0621.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[linux-kernel] 20031105 BK2CVS problem"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/8987","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"8987"},{"url":"http://www.ussg.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/0311.0/0630.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[linux-kernel] 20031105 Re: BK2CVS problem"},{"url":"http://www.ussg.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/0311.0/0627.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[linux-kernel] 20031105 Re: BK2CVS problem"}],"vendors":["linux-kernel"]}
{"id":"CVE-2003-1288","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-12-04T11:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-08T02:19:46.091Z","description":"Multiple race conditions in Linux-VServer 1.22 with Linux kernel 2.4.23 and SMP allow local users to cause a denial of service (kernel oops) via unknown attack vectors related to the (1) s_info and (2) ip_info data structures and the (a) forget_original_parent, (b) goodness, (c) schedule, (d) update_process_times, and (e) vc_new_s_context functions.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://linux-vserver.org/ChangeLog","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://list.linux-vserver.org/archive/vserver/msg05631.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[Vserver] 20031219 Re: SMP oops 2.4.23 v1.22"},{"url":"http://list.linux-vserver.org/archive/vserver/msg05658.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[Vserver] 20031220 Re: SMP oops 2.4.23 v1.22"},{"url":"http://list.linux-vserver.org/archive/vserver/msg05630.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[Vserver] 20031218 SMP oops 2.4.23 v1.22"},{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/7587","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"7587"}],"vendors":["linux-kernel"]}
{"id":"CVE-2003-1604","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"debian","published":"2016-05-02T10:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-08T02:35:17.578Z","description":"The redirect_target function in net/ipv4/netfilter/ipt_REDIRECT.c in the Linux kernel before 2.6.0 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (NULL pointer dereference and OOPS) by sending packets to an interface that has a 0.0.0.0 IP address, a related issue to CVE-2015-8787.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1303072","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=netfilter-devel&m=106668497403047&w=2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[netfilter-devel] 20031020 [PATCH] Fix possible oops in ipt_REDIRECT"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2016/01/27/9","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20160127 Re: CVE Request: Linux: NULL pointer dereference netfilter/nf_nat_redirect.c in nf_nat_redirect_ipv4 function"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2016-04/msg00015.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2016:1008"}],"vendors":["linux-kernel"]}
